// Document admin should require being an owner (directly, or via the
// owning organization's admin) — not just any random user. Pin the
// document's owner to a specific organization o, then ask whether an
// arbitrary user u gets admin without any pin tying u to o or its
// platform at all.
//
// Before `docs/DECISIONS.md`'s entry adding `NeverRelationConstraint`,
// this invariant's own real verdict was VIOLATED: nothing stopped the
// search from adding one more, wholly unconstrained direct grant of
// `document.owner_user` (bare principal) to `u` — the exact "recurring
// finding" `docs/FINDINGS.md` disclosed. A second, completely
// independent escape existed too, unrelated to `owner_user`: an
// unconstrained direct grant of `platform.administrator` to `u`,
// reachable via `owner_org->admin` since `o` is already pinned — nothing
// in this invariant's own givens ties `u` to that platform at all.
// `never document#owner_user(u)` and `never platform#administrator(u)`
// close both — `owner_org`'s own bare branch needs no line at all (its
// declared subject type is `organization`, never `user`, so it can never
// resolve `u` directly regardless). See `docs/FINDINGS.md` for the full
// account.
invariant document_admin_requires_ownership_chain {
  u: user
  o: organization
  d: document

  owner_org(d) = o

  never document#owner_user(u)
  never platform#administrator(u)

  goal: admin(u, d)
}
